WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.220 --> 00:00:05.259
So I sort of mentioned in passing in my story
about martial law earlier in the show that

00:00:05.259 --> 00:00:10.290
the mayor of Portland was teargassed along
with protesters recently by Donald Trump's

00:00:10.290 --> 00:00:14.760
federal troops operating under the banner
of homeland security.

00:00:14.760 --> 00:00:17.910
But I never really gave you the details of
what happened there.

00:00:17.910 --> 00:00:24.159
So not only was Portland Mayor Ted Wheeler
gassed, President Donald Trump seemed to brag

00:00:24.159 --> 00:00:25.269
about it.

00:00:25.269 --> 00:00:27.980
Here's Donald Trump during an outrageous Fox
News interview.

00:00:27.980 --> 00:00:30.119
First of all, notice Trump doesn't even know
the guy's name.

00:00:30.119 --> 00:00:31.720
His name is Ted Wheeler.

00:00:31.720 --> 00:00:34.910
Trump calls him Wailin and then Sean Hannity
corrects him.

00:00:34.910 --> 00:00:39.271
And then Trump brags about Wheeler getting
the hell knocked out of him.

00:00:39.271 --> 00:00:43.260
And it's not to be totally honest, it's not
clear if Trump's referring to getting tear

00:00:43.260 --> 00:00:45.480
gassed or that he was booed.

00:00:45.480 --> 00:00:47.430
But take a look at the clip and then we'll
discuss.

00:00:47.430 --> 00:00:53.410
Sen. They were going wild for fifty one days
and we went in and they've done a great job

00:00:53.410 --> 00:00:57.850
hunting trip down the courthouse as a big
federal courthouse, gorgeous federal courthouse.

00:00:57.850 --> 00:01:01.180
So we went in and we've been very, very strong
and we have this mayor.

00:01:01.180 --> 00:01:02.180
Well and I think he's also, he's also the
police commissioner as I understand it, Dale

00:01:02.180 --> 00:01:03.180
Aadland, Mayor Wheeler.

00:01:03.180 --> 00:01:12.220
And he's he made a fool out of himself as
he wanted to be among the people.

00:01:12.220 --> 00:01:17.910
So he went into the crowd and they knocked
the hell out of him.

00:01:17.910 --> 00:01:20.260
That was the end of him.

00:01:20.260 --> 00:01:21.659
So it was pretty, pretty pathetic.

00:01:21.659 --> 00:01:25.460
But we want to go in and help the cities.

00:01:25.460 --> 00:01:26.460
We want to help Chicago.

00:01:26.460 --> 00:01:29.799
So, indeed, a few days ago, Ted Wheeler was
hit with tear gas while he was standing with

00:01:29.799 --> 00:01:32.010
protesters near the courthouse.

00:01:32.010 --> 00:01:38.440
And just about everything Trump says in that
very short clip is false.

00:01:38.440 --> 00:01:43.229
Trump calls the mayor, Wheelin Hannity corrects
him so he gets the guy's name wrong.

00:01:43.229 --> 00:01:47.210
Trump says that protesters were going wild
for 51 days.

00:01:47.210 --> 00:01:48.650
That's certainly not true.

00:01:48.650 --> 00:01:54.190
Again, unless Donald Trump is actually, you
know, some kind of physicist that has a different

00:01:54.190 --> 00:01:55.960
conception of what time means.

00:01:55.960 --> 00:01:59.840
By no measure have the protesters been going
wild for 51 days.

00:01:59.840 --> 00:02:03.130
Trump says the courthouse was going to be
ripped down.

00:02:03.130 --> 00:02:04.729
That's not true.

00:02:04.729 --> 00:02:12.120
But the really shocking thing here is that
it is so dictatorial and so authoritarian

00:02:12.120 --> 00:02:18.690
that Trump is ridiculing Ted Wheeler for being
on the side of the public against the federal

00:02:18.690 --> 00:02:19.850
paramilitaries.

00:02:19.850 --> 00:02:24.470
In other words, overwhelmingly, people don't
want these federal troops in Portland.

00:02:24.470 --> 00:02:29.400
Now, I've gotten a couple e-mails over the
weekend from people saying, you know, David,

00:02:29.400 --> 00:02:32.739
you should see that there are like individuals.

00:02:32.739 --> 00:02:39.400
Someone told me, although I haven't confirmed
that Brett Weinstein wants the troops there

00:02:39.400 --> 00:02:43.160
because he says, you know, the rest of the
country doesn't really understand what's going

00:02:43.160 --> 00:02:44.160
on.

00:02:44.160 --> 00:02:45.160
I don't.

00:02:45.160 --> 00:02:46.160
I don't know if that's true.

00:02:46.160 --> 00:02:47.160
I got a few e-mails about that.

00:02:47.160 --> 00:02:50.200
Overwhelmingly, people don't want these troops
there.

00:02:50.200 --> 00:02:52.850
The mayor doesn't want the troops there.

00:02:52.850 --> 00:02:57.220
And the local law enforcement authorities
are not working in conjunction with these

00:02:57.220 --> 00:03:01.260
troops and anything that would be called a
cooperative way.

00:03:01.260 --> 00:03:04.520
And the mayor, as the citizen is joining the
people.

00:03:04.520 --> 00:03:05.520
That's great.

00:03:05.520 --> 00:03:08.240
Now, yeah, the mayor was booed by some people
when he did this.

00:03:08.240 --> 00:03:11.720
And that relates to, you know, people may
be displeased with the mayor's handling of

00:03:11.720 --> 00:03:17.470
the situation, but shouldn't we like it when
elected officials instead of hanging out in

00:03:17.470 --> 00:03:19.390
the safety of their ivory towers?

00:03:19.390 --> 00:03:21.890
If Portland has our ivory towers, I don't
know.

00:03:21.890 --> 00:03:23.709
And making declarations.

00:03:23.709 --> 00:03:29.920
Wouldn't it be better if people were joined
by elected officials?

00:03:29.920 --> 00:03:31.010
Isn't that what we want to see?

00:03:31.010 --> 00:03:35.480
Now, I know that there will be situations
where it doesn't feel genuine.

00:03:35.480 --> 00:03:41.269
And when Mitt Romney, a Republican senator,
joined the Black Lives Matter protests wearing

00:03:41.269 --> 00:03:46.520
a mask, no less in Washington, D.C., joining
mostly left wingers, let's be honest about

00:03:46.520 --> 00:03:47.520
it.

00:03:47.520 --> 00:03:49.090
And he was asked, what are you doing here,
Senator?

00:03:49.090 --> 00:03:50.830
He said, I'm here because Black Lives Matter.

00:03:50.830 --> 00:03:52.860
And he kept his mask on and he did it.

00:03:52.860 --> 00:03:55.830
There were people who said, this is disingenuous,
Romney.

00:03:55.830 --> 00:03:58.090
This is the guy who is going to lower taxes
on millionaires.

00:03:58.090 --> 00:03:59.489
Oh, yeah, that's true.

00:03:59.489 --> 00:04:00.489
It's it's Romney.

00:04:00.489 --> 00:04:01.489
It is that guy.

00:04:01.489 --> 00:04:03.080
He's still a Republican.

00:04:03.080 --> 00:04:08.769
But I think it's important when a Republican
says, hey, I have to choose the movement over

00:04:08.769 --> 00:04:11.010
my party in this particular case.

00:04:11.010 --> 00:04:14.940
I think that it should be applauded, but with
some healthy skepticism that these are still

00:04:14.940 --> 00:04:17.430
politicians who are calculating what they
do.

00:04:17.430 --> 00:04:24.120
The point is, we should be glad when elected
officials join movements rather than just

00:04:24.120 --> 00:04:27.770
sending out messages on Twitter or hanging
out in their office.

00:04:27.770 --> 00:04:32.750
And Donald Trump is ridiculing Ted Wheeler
for hearing the voice of the people and joining

00:04:32.750 --> 00:04:34.660
them in their peaceful protests.

00:04:34.660 --> 00:04:39.880
This isn't getting that much attention, but
it is insanely authoritarian.

00:04:39.880 --> 00:04:45.729
The president sits in D.C. and essentially
laughs at a public servant who is joining

00:04:45.729 --> 00:04:48.880
people and says he got the hell knocked out
of them.

00:04:48.880 --> 00:04:49.880
Again, it's not.

00:04:49.880 --> 00:04:50.880
Was that from.

00:04:50.880 --> 00:04:53.229
He was teargassed, but it's not clear if Trump
was referring to that.

00:04:53.229 --> 00:04:56.050
So we have to recognize this for what it is.

00:04:56.050 --> 00:04:59.560
And to follow up on the earlier story about.

00:04:59.560 --> 00:05:01.650
Martial law and authoritarianism.

00:05:01.650 --> 00:05:06.800
Federal troops are being sent around to different
cities, a growing list of cities to satisfy.

00:05:06.800 --> 00:05:13.250
Donald Trump's whims and to, as Trump sees
it, generate chaos that will help get him

00:05:13.250 --> 00:05:14.430
reelected.

00:05:14.430 --> 00:05:16.090
We just can't allow it to work.

00:05:16.090 --> 00:05:21.620
But this is his plan now to get ahead of a
narrative that's being floated already.

00:05:21.620 --> 00:05:27.690
If you look in some reactionary and Right-Wing
circles there, you might be shocked by this.

00:05:27.690 --> 00:05:33.400
There are some right wingers abandoning their
so-called small government values and saying,

00:05:33.400 --> 00:05:40.080
I support the paramilitaries because these
protesters deserve it because they are criminals.

00:05:40.080 --> 00:05:42.280
Again, the protesters aren't criminals.

00:05:42.280 --> 00:05:44.700
They are protesters.

00:05:44.700 --> 00:05:47.210
They are constitutionally protected.

00:05:47.210 --> 00:05:48.380
It is speech.

00:05:48.380 --> 00:05:50.370
They are peaceably assembling.

00:05:50.370 --> 00:05:56.630
And they are asking for the redress of grievances
that they are bringing forward.

00:05:56.630 --> 00:06:00.759
If they are criminals, then they are criminals,
right?

00:06:00.759 --> 00:06:02.420
Protesters aren't criminals.

00:06:02.420 --> 00:06:03.699
Protesters are the patriots here.

00:06:03.699 --> 00:06:05.949
And that's the something the right doesn't
want to accept.

00:06:05.949 --> 00:06:10.139
The right has attempted to hold the monopoly
on patriotism in the United States for a long

00:06:10.139 --> 00:06:11.139
time.

00:06:11.139 --> 00:06:14.380
Certainly, I was most exposed to it around
the 2003 Iraq war.

00:06:14.380 --> 00:06:15.380
But it's not new.

00:06:15.380 --> 00:06:17.389
It's been going on for decades and decades.

00:06:17.389 --> 00:06:20.170
The protesters are being patriotic.

00:06:20.170 --> 00:06:24.389
They are doing the things that our country
was enshrined upon.

00:06:24.389 --> 00:06:26.340
A protester is not a criminal.

00:06:26.340 --> 00:06:29.310
Now, I've said before, and I'll repeat it.

00:06:29.310 --> 00:06:30.539
Some of you disagree.

00:06:30.539 --> 00:06:33.710
Breaking windows at a courthouse is not going
to forward any cause.

00:06:33.710 --> 00:06:34.710
And it is a crime.

00:06:34.710 --> 00:06:38.400
And you're going to be suffering the consequences
of committing a crime if you do it.

00:06:38.400 --> 00:06:42.240
Setting fires to buildings is not going to
further any cause.

00:06:42.240 --> 00:06:43.240
And it's a crime.

00:06:43.240 --> 00:06:47.240
And you should expect that if you do that,
you are going to be arrested and charged.

00:06:47.240 --> 00:06:48.930
And it could be really bad for you.

00:06:48.930 --> 00:06:50.979
Martin Luther King was very clear about this.

00:06:50.979 --> 00:06:55.520
Martin, there's some very interesting contrast,
lookup videos of interviews with Martin Luther

00:06:55.520 --> 00:07:01.380
King and separately with Malcolm X, both of
whom were bringing a lot of different ideas,

00:07:01.380 --> 00:07:03.610
forward, valuable ideas.

00:07:03.610 --> 00:07:08.440
Martin Luther King differed from Malcolm X
and that Martin Luther King recognized that

00:07:08.440 --> 00:07:15.360
when you start using more violent tactics
are seen, destruction of property, etc., even

00:07:15.360 --> 00:07:19.270
if you can morally defend it, even if we can
all say an insurance company will pay to rebuild

00:07:19.270 --> 00:07:20.520
the building, who cares?

00:07:20.520 --> 00:07:25.480
OK, that's aside from the fact that people
could get hurt or killed as bystanders.

00:07:25.480 --> 00:07:31.540
Martin Luther King pointed out it often comes
back to hurt exactly the people doing the

00:07:31.540 --> 00:07:32.590
protesting.

00:07:32.590 --> 00:07:37.479
And when you consider that many of these protests
are overwhelmingly white.

00:07:37.479 --> 00:07:43.900
Do we really improve the situation for the
people that we are most trying to help by

00:07:43.900 --> 00:07:49.139
introducing elements of violence here, which
may only lead to even rougher treatment by

00:07:49.139 --> 00:07:51.580
police of the very people we are trying to
help?

00:07:51.580 --> 00:07:53.160
So I do see that as self-destructive.

00:07:53.160 --> 00:07:54.450
Right.

00:07:54.450 --> 00:07:58.720
This is not a show where if you're tuning
in for me to defend criminality, that's not

00:07:58.720 --> 00:08:00.010
this show.

00:08:00.010 --> 00:08:01.990
But most of the people are just protesters.

00:08:01.990 --> 00:08:05.690
It's moms now who have showed up to back up
the protesters.

00:08:05.690 --> 00:08:10.849
And then veterans showed up to back up the
moms who were backing up the protesters.

00:08:10.849 --> 00:08:12.470
So we can't let them set.

00:08:12.470 --> 00:08:17.259
The narrative of the troops are fine because
it's really mostly criminals there and the

00:08:17.259 --> 00:08:18.560
protesters are criminals.

00:08:18.560 --> 00:08:22.560
Now, we can't let them set that narrative
and not letting them set the narrative is

00:08:22.560 --> 00:09:04.300
just part of part of what we need to be doing
for the

00:09:04.300 --> 00:09:53.639
next three months.

